    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Builds acquisition cohorts from activity or order data and measures retention and revenue per cohort over time, with an average retention curve.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Marketing",
    "tags": [
        "cohort",
        "retention",
        "churn",
        "lifetime value",
        "subscription",
        "saas",
        "e-commerce",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Answers the questions every subscription, app and e-commerce business asks: *how many of the customers we won in March are still with us?* and *are newer customers sticking better than older ones?*\n\nEach customer belongs to the **cohort** of the period (week, month, quarter, year) of their first activity. For each cohort and each later period the block counts the customers still active, so you get:\n\n- the **cohort matrix** (long format, ready for a Pivot table or heat map): cohort, period number (0 = acquisition period), active customers, **retention %**, and if a revenue field is chosen, revenue, revenue per cohort customer and **cumulative revenue per customer** (a simple lifetime value curve)\n- the **average retention curve** across cohorts (weighted by cohort size, and the plain mean of cohorts)\n- a **customer table**: cohort, last active period, periods active, active in the latest period\n\nPeriods with no activity count as zero; recent cohorts simply have fewer periods. Input is any table with a customer and a date per activity or order.",
